{:edb/db-before-t 539 :edb/db-after-t 540 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533852 50 #inst "2026-10-05T03:49:32.129Z" 13194139533852 true] [17592186210488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255496 13194139533852 true] [17592186212940 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255489 13194139533852 true] [17592186212940 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255497 13194139533852 true] [17592186212940 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255504 13194139533852 true] [17592186212940 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255511 13194139533852 true] [17592186212941 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255515 13194139533852 true] [17592186212941 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255522 13194139533852 true] [17592186212941 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255529 13194139533852 true] [17592186212941 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255533 13194139533852 true] [17592186212941 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255536 13194139533852 true] [17592186212942 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255539 13194139533852 true] [17592186212942 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255546 13194139533852 true] [17592186212942 1020 #edb/ref 17592186255549 13194139533852 true] [17592186213376 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533852 true] [17592186213376 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the linear terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $b.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $9.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nb=9.\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186213380 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533852 true] [17592186213380 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means that after distributing $k$ on the left-hand side, the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nk({x}^{2}+7x+10)=k{x}^{2}+7kx+10k\n$$\n\nThis must equal the right-hand side. So, we have\n\n$$\nk{x}^{2}+7kx+10k=5{x}^{2}+35x+50.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms. \n\nComparing the ${x}^{2}$ terms, we have\n\n$$\nk=5.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that value $k=5$ produces the correct linear coefficient and constant term:\n\n- $7k=7(5)=35\\,✓$\n\n- $10k=10(5)=50\\,✓$\n\nSo, our solution is valid." 13194139533852 true] [17592186213381 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533852 true] [17592186213381 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ax+4)(x+b) & =a{x}^{2}+abx+4x+4b \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}+(ab+4)x+4b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+(ab+4)x+4b=2{x}^{2}+14x+20.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\na=2.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n4b=20\\,⇒\\,b=5.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $a=2$ and $b=5$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ab+4 & =2\\cdot 5+4 \\\\  & =10+4 \\\\  & =14\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $a+b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =2+5 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255489 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255490 13194139533852 true] [17592186255489 1089 "q-288051" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255489 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533852 true] [17592186255489 1100 "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2x+c={x}^{2}+2x+5\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $c?$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255489 1113 #uuid "e1c9c830-4c7c-525c-ab10-8752098cfbe0" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255489 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the constant terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the constant is $c.$ On the right-hand side, the constant is $5.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nc=5.\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255491 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255492 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255493 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255494 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255495 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1041 "selection" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255495 13194139533852 true] [17592186255490 1110 #uuid "443196e8-2fdd-5df0-998e-da53d8476756" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255491 1034 "3" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255491 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255491 1111 #uuid "b7f74c8a-6c5d-58de-9068-4624d614ccd9" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255492 1034 "2" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255492 1111 #uuid "c430f780-eaf0-5c8f-a42d-bf2d2637b0c7" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255493 1034 "1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255493 1111 #uuid "1fd08dbe-e60a-5fcb-ada9-c38a3499b7cd" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255494 1034 "0" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255494 1111 #uuid "16e383a3-f5b8-5cc9-9cee-8416077b3ca4" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255495 1034 "5" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255495 1111 #uuid "af0be384-2419-503e-b23a-fcfe000f1f8b" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255496 1034 "6" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255496 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255496 1111 #uuid "67d06be6-5ae9-5aa9-9041-90