7592186045449 13194139533852 true] [17592186255512 1041 "field-1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255512 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255514 13194139533852 true] [17592186255512 1110 #uuid "0badedaf-efa3-504f-a7fa-bec469764e32" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255513 1034 "2" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255513 1111 #uuid "90b98ad6-0d26-5417-8a5f-23b1652dfcd4" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255514 1034 "-2" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255514 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255514 1111 #uuid "d8d68d17-b4d2-5609-8bc9-032941933f05" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255515 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255516 13194139533852 true] [17592186255515 1089 "q-288451" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255515 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533852 true] [17592186255515 1100 "The equation \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+mx+c={x}^{2}+7x-5\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $m$ and $c$ are constants. What is the value of $m+c?$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255515 1113 #uuid "cbe86354-6280-5067-a456-42950cdfd26a" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255515 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $m,$ and on the right-hand side it is $7.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nm=7.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $c,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-5.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nc=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+c & =7+(-5) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255517 13194139533852 true] [17592186255516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255518 13194139533852 true] [17592186255516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255519 13194139533852 true] [17592186255516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255520 13194139533852 true] [17592186255516 1000 #edb/ref 175921