533852 true] [17592186255536 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ on the left-hand side is $u,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-7.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nu=-7.\n$$\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $v,$ and on the right-hand side it is $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nv=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =(-7)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255538 13194139533852 true] [17592186255537 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533852 true] [17592186255537 1041 "field-1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255537 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255538 13194139533852 true] [17592186255537 1110 #uuid "1888d438-714b-5154-b9be-b524b7304b1c" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255538 1034 "-7" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255538 1111 #uuid "9c4440ff-6fcf-5796-8092-e168dfb8d9df" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255539 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255540 13194139533852 true] [17592186255539 1089 "q-288468" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255539 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533852 true] [17592186255539 1100 "The equation\n\n$$\nt(2{x}^{2}-3x+1)=-6{x}^{2}+9x-3\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $t$ is a constant. What is the value of $t?$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255539 1113 #uuid "9f05ef00-ecf3-521e-8eb7-f45de3139297" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255539 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means that after distributing $t$ on the left-hand side, the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nt(2{x}^{2}-3x+1)=2t{x}^{2}-3tx+t\n$$\n\nThis must equal the right-hand side. So, we have\n\n$$\n2t{x}^{2}-3tx+t=-6{x}^{2}+9x-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms. \n\nComparing the ${x}^{2}$ terms, we have\n\n$$\n2t=-6\\,⇒\\,t=-3.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that value $t=-3$ produces the correct linear coefficient and constant term:\n\n- $-3t=(-3)(-3)=9\\,✓$\n\n- $t=-3\\,✓$\n\nSo, our solution is valid." 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255541 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255542 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255543 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255544 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255545 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1041 "selection" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255545 13194139533852 true] [17592186255540 1110 #uuid "daebb1a6-92f0-59cf-bff5-b5367267f8bc" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255541 1034 "3" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255541 1111 #uuid "07c8222b-75e0-5775-84d3-f1224424ed81" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255542 1034 "2" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255542 1111 #uuid "dd68e33a-5c52-5923-97ab-e722a61e4fca" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255543 1034 "6" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255543 1111 #uuid "dfbe5945-bfff-52d7-a503-35996d529bf6" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255544 1034 "1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255544 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255544 1111 #uuid "9e55d357-4249-5383-84bb-727fa1e29284" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255545 1034 "-3" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255545 1111 #uuid "f4545191-d3a5-58f8-8bd2-c496a9006f2a" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255546 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255547 13194139533852 true] [17592186255546 1089 "q-288697" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255546 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533852 true] [17592186255546 1100 "The equation \n\n$$\n(cx-8)(x+d)=4{x}^{2}-20x+24\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $c$ and $d$ are constants.What is the value of $c+d?$\n\n$c+d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255546 1113 #uuid "c020a0c1-43c7-514c-b47c-f3c429e8e8cf" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255546 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(cx-8)(x+d) & =c{x}^{2}+cdx-8x-8d \\\\  & =c{x}^{2}+(cd-8)x-8d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nc{x}^{2}+(cd-8)x-8d=4{x}^{2}-20x+24.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\nc=4.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n-8d=24\\,⇒\\,d=-3.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $c=4$ and $d=-3$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cd-8 & =4\\cdot (-3)-8 \\\\  & =-12-8 \\\\  & =-20\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $c+d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c+d & =4+(-3) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255547 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255548 13194139533852 true] [17592186255547 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533852 true] [17592186255547 1041 "field-1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255547 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255548 13194139533852 true] [17592186255547 1110 #uuid "6164c4c1-c223-5f65-b959-f84fc20d982f" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255548 1034 "1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533852 true] [17592186255548 1111 #uuid "3f0e7d6d-7f8f-5fc4-b1b6-a416d2781d28" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255549 1017 #edb/ref 17592186255550 13194139533852 true] [17592186255549 1089 "q-288698" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255549 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533852 true] [17592186255549 1100 "The equation\n\n$$\n(mx+10)(x+n)=-5{x}^{2}+20x-20\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $m$ and $n$ are constants. What is the value of $m+n?$\n\n$m+n=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255549 1113 #uuid "e2b02957-533e-54ac-94ee-103972717b02" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255549 1145 "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(mx+10)(x+n) & =m{x}^{2}+mnx+10x+10n \\\\  & =m{x}^{2}+(mn+10)x+10n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nm{x}^{2}+(mn+10)x+10n=-5{x}^{2}+20x-20.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\nm=-5.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n10n=-20\\,⇒\\,n=-2.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $m=-5$ and $n=-2$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}mn+10 & =(-5)(-2)+10 \\\\  & =10+10 \\\\  & =20\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $m+n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+n & =-5+(-2) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255550 1000 #edb/ref 17592186255551 13194139533852 true] [17592186255550 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533852 true] [17592186255550 1041 "field-1" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255550 1104 #edb/ref 17592186255551 13194139533852 true] [17592186255550 1110 #uuid "78b6324b-22fe-5284-8b6c-f377ca83ad25" 13194139533852 true] [17592186255551 1034 "-